│ patch_name               │ checkerboard_mixer                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ This update replaces the fully uniform block with a parity-aware “checkerboard” mixer     │
│                          │ that is lighter but more expressive in the right places.                                  │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key ideas:                                                                                │
│                          │ - Keep parameter sharing strong to preserve generalization and parameter efficiency.      │
│                          │ - Split the input and output mixers into even/odd wire groups so the circuit can learn    │
│                          │ asymmetric structure without exploding the parameter count.                               │
│                          │ - Replace the all-CZ entangling scaffold with a CZ + CNOT ladder, which is better suited  │
│                          │ for converting the fixed ZZ feature-map phases into measurable Z-basis signal.            │
│                          │ - Remove redundant full-width single-qubit layers and reduce gate count per block         │
│                          │ substantially, which should help the combined score while keeping the ansatz trainable.   │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This keeps the fixed architecture intact and only changes ANSATZ_SPEC, as required.       │
