│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_parameterized_entanglement                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current program achieves excellent results (0.90 test accuracy, very low              │
│                          │ generalization gap, high parameter efficiency with only 26 params) through aggressive     │
│                          │ parameter sharing with collective layers. However, the gate count is high (348) relative  │
│                          │ to the parameter count, suggesting the structure is very efficient but potentially        │
│                          │ limited in expressiveness.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ To improve further, I propose adding a parameterized two-qubit layer using selective CRZ  │
│                          │ gates in a complementary pattern to the existing fixed CZ entanglement. This introduces   │
│                          │ controlled parameterized interactions while maintaining the efficient shared parameter    │
│                          │ structure. The new layer will:                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. Add 4 parameterized CRZ gates using complementary diagonal pairs: [0,3], [1,4], [2,5], │
│                          │ [6,7]                                                                                     │
│                          │ 2. Use a shared parameter "param_cz" for all 4 CRZ gates to keep the parameter count low  │
│                          │ while increasing expressiveness                                                           │
│                          │ 3. Place this layer after the fixed CZ entangler to allow both fixed and parameterized    │
│                          │ interactions                                                                              │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This approach:                                                                            │
│                          │ - Increases expressiveness by allowing tunable entanglement on complementary pairs        │
│                          │ - Keeps parameter growth minimal (only +1 param per block = +6 params total)              │
│                          │ - Maintains the proven symmetry benefits of collective parameter sharing                  │
│                          │ - Complements rather than replaces the existing fixed CZ pattern                          │
